# The DEFAULT ignore file for the repository-root build context.
#
# ★ Both images build from the root, because both need `packages/contracts` and
# the workspace lockfile. This file excludes what neither needs.
#
# ★★ Each Dockerfile also has its own `<path>.dockerignore` beside it, which
# BuildKit prefers over this one when present. That is how `apps/web` can be
# excluded from the API's context — it is several hundred megabytes the API
# never reads — while the web build still sees it. Before those files existed
# the web image failed with `"/apps/web": not found`, which reads like a missing
# directory rather than an ignore rule.

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Its own dependency tree, deliberately outside the workspace.
docs/spikes

docs
*.md
!apps/api/assets/fonts/README.md

**/coverage
**/.vitest
